## Authelia — Self-hosted Reverse-Proxy Auth

Single-binary Go service. Sits in front of your services as a forward-auth middleware. Lightweight alternative to Keycloak.

### docker-compose.authelia.yml

```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  authelia:
    image: authelia/authelia:latest
    container_name: authelia
    ports:
      - '9091:9091'
    volumes:
      - ./authelia/config:/config
      - authelia-data:/var/lib/authelia/storage
    environment:
      - AUTHELIA_JWT_SECRET=<random-secret>
      - AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET=<random-secret>
      - AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<random-secret>
    restart: unless-stopped

  traefik:
    image: traefik:v3
    container_name: traefik
    ports:
      - '80:80'
      - '443:443'
    volumes:
      - ./traefik/traefik.yml:/etc/traefik/traefik.yml:ro
      - /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock:ro
    depends_on: [authelia]
    restart: unless-stopped

volumes:
  authelia-data:
```

### authelia/config/configuration.yml (minimal)

```yaml
server:
  host: 0.0.0.0
  port: 9091

authentication_backend:
  file:
    path: /config/users_database.yml

access_control:
  default_policy: deny
  rules:
    - domain: '<%= projectName %>.local'
      policy: one_factor

session:
  secret: ${AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET}
  domain: '<%= projectName %>.local'

storage:
  local:
    path: /var/lib/authelia/storage/db.sqlite3
```

### Environment variables

```env
AUTHELIA_JWT_SECRET=<random-32-char-secret>
AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET=<random-32-char-secret>
AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<random-32-char-secret>
```
