## Keycloak — Self-hosted Enterprise SSO

Java/Quarkus-based. The heavyweight reference stack. Best for enterprise SSO with complex customization requirements.

### docker-compose.keycloak.yml

```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  keycloak:
    image: quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:latest
    container_name: keycloak
    ports:
      - '8180:8080'
    command: start-dev
    environment:
      KEYCLOAK_ADMIN: admin
      KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD: ${KC_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
      KC_DB: postgres
      KC_DB_URL: jdbc:postgresql://postgresql:5432/keycloak
      KC_DB_USERNAME: keycloak
      KC_DB_PASSWORD: ${PG_PASS}
    depends_on: [postgresql]
    restart: unless-stopped

  postgresql:
    image: postgres:16
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: keycloak
      POSTGRES_USER: keycloak
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${PG_PASS}
    volumes:
      - kc-db:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    restart: unless-stopped

volumes:
  kc-db:
```

### Realm export / import

```bash
# Export realm config for version control
docker exec keycloak /opt/keycloak/bin/kc.sh export \
  --realm <%= projectName %> \
  --dir /tmp/realm-export \
  --users realm_file

# Import on fresh deployment
docker exec keycloak /opt/keycloak/bin/kc.sh import \
  --dir /tmp/realm-export
```

### OIDC integration (Node.js)

```typescript
import KcAdminClient from '@keycloak/keycloak-admin-client'
import { Issuer } from 'openid-client'

const issuer = await Issuer.discover(
